  "observations": "Native string, arguments, file/stream, namespace/escaping, xml:base/xml:id subset and edge-argument receipts. Scalar or empty-string XPath gives the whole document; Boolean false and Structure filter give empty output. Conversion mechanism is not inferred; Namespace snapshot returns four DOM XPath namespace objects with the recorded native property presentations; positions beyond the snapshot return Undefined. An empty DOM document canonicalizes successfully to the empty string in the separate completed native control; the earlier combined timeout is not evidence of a canonicalizer hang. Boolean false and Structure filters still produce empty output when the document root is named exactly by the native String(value) presentation (No and Structure); ordinary string-to-XPath coercion is therefore not established. Eight xml:base combinations measured for each of the six algorithms, including parent/child paths, absolute path/URI, query, fragment, empty value and relative chain. Passed XPathResult values (single-element node set, Number, Boolean and String) retain the full document in all four recorded controls. Numeric filename 1 is accepted; numeric stream receiver, closed memory stream and element instead of DOM document are rejected. Ten URI edge combinations measured for each algorithm: origin without path, root clamping, network path, terminal dot/parent, double slash collapse, unchanged absolute URI dot segments, relative leading parents and urn scheme.",
